.TH SLIDER 1
.SH NAME
slider \- writing a control
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B temple/slider
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Slider
is a port of the TempleOS
.B Demo/Graphics/Slider.HC
demonstration.
It runs under
.IR wm (1).
.PP
"It's conceptually easy to do a ctrl, but tedious.  You have complete
freedom."  A control in TempleOS is four function pointers and a state
blob \- draw, click, update-derived-values, and flags asking for the mouse
\- and an editor template writes all of that out so you need only fill in
the drawing.  This one is two vertical sliders in a red-bordered blue box
with their values 0 to 10 printed beneath.  The update-derived-values
call re-centres the control and clamps its positions whenever the window
changes, which is what keeps a control honest across a resize.
.PP
The controls are:
.TF "any key"
.TP
.B LMB
Move a slider
.TP
.B "any key"
Read the values, then exit
.PD
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/temple/slider.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR temple (1),
.IR wm (1)
